
PROJECT: AICTE SECURITY DEPOSIT / FDR MANAGEMENT SYSTEM

IMPORTANT CONTEXT:

The initial project foundation and application UI have already
been created.

Continue working on the EXISTING project.

Do not recreate the application from scratch.
Do not destroy or replace the existing architecture.
Do not remove existing working components.
Inspect the current codebase, identify the existing routes,
components, database configuration and design system, and
extend them.

PROJECT OBJECTIVE:

Transform the existing application into a complete,
professional, highly interactive, fully functional prototype
for managing Security Deposits and Fixed Deposit Receipts (FDRs)
for AICTE and AICTE-approved technical institutions.

This is a demonstration prototype.

Mock data, simulated bank verification, simulated email
notifications and simulated approval integrations are allowed.

However, every visible feature must have working interactions.
Buttons must perform meaningful actions.
Forms must validate.
Tables must support search and filtering.
Status changes must update the application.
Workflows must connect across modules.
Changes must persist during the demonstration.

Do not build a static dashboard or a collection of disconnected
screens.

